Kreative Studio pose editor (STU-PE1). Plain JavaScript, no libraries, no build step. The same file runs in Node 22 (CommonJS require) and in the browser (classic <script>, no modules). Use exactly this wrapper and nothing outside it:

(function () {
  'use strict';
  const NS = typeof module === 'object' && module.exports ? null : (globalThis.KKPose = globalThis.KKPose || {});
  const need = (name, file) => (NS ? NS[name] : require(file));
  // ... the code; get other pose modules with need('vec', './vec.js') INSIDE functions (load order in the browser is free) ...
  const api = { /* exported names */ };
  if (NS) NS.<NAME> = api; else module.exports = api;
})();

Angles are degrees in every API. Coordinates are metres: +X is the figure's left, -Y its front, +Z up. Matrices are arrays of 9 numbers, row-major. Do not change the test file.


Write lib/pose-api.js for Kreative Studio (Node 22, CommonJS, Express 4): the pose editor's HTTP API. This file is NOT a browser file: plain CommonJS with require at the top, no wrapper. It exports { poseRouter, renderPose }.

Requires: express, fs/promises as fs, path, crypto, zlib, and the pose modules '../public/js/pose/<name>.js' for skeleton (S), fk (FK), ops (OPS), presets (PR), project (P), raster (R), draw-openpose (D, its function is D.drawOpenPose), depth (DEPTH).

renderPose(pose, view): w = FK.solve(pose); v = P.makeView(view, w); kp = P.keypoints(v, w); a = R.create(v.width, v.height); D.drawOpenPose(a, kp); b = R.create(v.width, v.height); DEPTH.render(v, w, b); return { openpose: Buffer.from(R.encodePNG(a, zlib.deflateSync)), depth: Buffer.from(R.encodePNG(b, zlib.deflateSync)), keypoints: P.openposeJSON(kp), view: { yaw: view.yaw || 0, pitch: view.pitch || 0, width: v.width, height: v.height, scale: v.scale, center: v.center } }.

Helpers inside the file:
- checkPose(pose): undefined/null -> FK.defaultPose(); an object with version === 1 -> pose; else throw a 400 error 'pose must be a version 1 pose.'.
- checkView(view = {}): width = view.width ?? 512, height = view.height ?? 768; both must be integers from 64 to 2048, else 400 'width and height must be whole numbers from 64 to 2048.'; return {...view, width, height}.
- A 400 error is an Error with .status = 400; routes catch errors and answer res.status(e.status || 500).json({ error: e.message }).
- Saved poses live in path.join(dataDir, 'poses', req.userId, id) with files meta.json, openpose.png, depth.png, keypoints.json. A valid id matches /^[0-9a-f-]{36}$/; anything else is 404 { error: 'No such pose.' } like a missing folder.

poseRouter({ dataDir }) returns an express.Router() with (req.userId and req.userEmail are set by the app before it):
- GET /pose/info -> { presets: PR.NAMES, ops: ['set_joint','curl_finger','mirror','look_at','ik','move_root','reset','preset'], joints: S.JOINTS.filter(j => j.aim !== null).map(j => ({ name: j.name, limits: j.limits })) }.
- POST /pose/ops { pose, ops } -> ops must be an array or a non-null object that is not an array, else 400 'ops must be an op object or a list of them.'; pose = checkPose(body.pose); OPS.apply errors (unknown op, bad joint ...) are 400 with their message; 200 { pose, notes }.
- POST /pose/render { pose, view } -> r = renderPose(checkPose(pose), checkView(view)); 200 { openpose: 'data:image/png;base64,' + r.openpose.toString('base64'), depth: same for r.depth, keypoints: r.keypoints, view: r.view }.
- GET /poses -> { poses: [...] } every meta.json of the user's folder (a missing folder is an empty list), newest provenance.created first.
- POST /poses { name, pose, view, provenance } -> name = String(name || '').trim(), 1 to 80 characters, else 400 'Give the pose a name (up to 80 characters).'; pose = checkPose(pose); view = checkView(view); id = crypto.randomUUID(); r = renderPose(pose, view); meta = { id, name, pose, view: r.view, provenance: { source: String(provenance?.source || 'editor'), ops: Array.isArray(provenance?.ops) ? provenance.ops : [], parent: provenance?.parent || null, by: req.userEmail, created: new Date().toISOString() } }; mkdir recursive, write meta.json, openpose.png, depth.png, keypoints.json (JSON); 201 { id }.
- GET /poses/:id -> the meta.json object.
- GET /poses/:id/:file -> file must be one of openpose.png, depth.png, keypoints.json, else 404 { error: 'No such file.' }; res.sendFile(full path) (Express sets image/png and application/json from the extension).
- DELETE /poses/:id -> fs.rm(folder, { recursive: true, force: true }); 200 { ok: true }.
